1
00:00:00,009 --> 00:00:03,509
Kofflard starts with one question: who do you like?

2
00:00:04,138 --> 00:00:05,958
Say, Nick Drake.

3
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:10,200
Kofflard asks an AI for musicians you may not know yet.

4
00:00:10,208 --> 00:00:13,870
Twelve of them, in three lanes.

5
00:00:17,442 --> 00:00:23,150
Close ones first. Then stretches. Then a few leaps.

6
00:00:27,047 --> 00:00:30,467
Close: the same quiet folk, well chosen.

7
00:00:30,471 --> 00:00:34,467
A stretch: less known, another year, the same feeling.

8
00:00:34,473 --> 00:00:37,781
And a leap: Ali Farka Touré, from Mali.

9
00:00:37,865 --> 00:00:42,005
Every leap says why: the same soft, looping fingerpicking.

10
00:00:42,014 --> 00:00:46,058
Relevance first. Surprise, but never out of the blue.

11
00:00:50,007 --> 00:00:52,125
One tap opens YouTube.

12
00:00:52,132 --> 00:00:54,856
Or Spotify, or YouTube Music.

13
00:00:54,865 --> 00:01:01,613
On a phone, in the app. On Windows, in the browser.

14
00:01:06,114 --> 00:01:07,934
Like Bill Fay?

15
00:01:07,983 --> 00:01:11,099
Follow him, and the next twelve start from there.

16
00:01:11,431 --> 00:01:15,333
Even a leap to Talk Talk, by way of the same hymn-like piano.

17
00:01:17,739 --> 00:01:19,559
Some names are shared.

18
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:22,646
Kofflard asks which one you mean.

19
00:01:22,658 --> 00:01:27,166
Genesis Owusu, then.

20
00:01:29,758 --> 00:01:31,578
Spotify more your thing?

21
00:01:36,239 --> 00:01:38,355
Make it the main button, everywhere.

22
00:01:38,366 --> 00:01:40,706
There is no Kofflard server.

23
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,420
Bring your own AI.

24
00:01:46,427 --> 00:01:52,407
Azure first; or OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, or a sign-in with OpenRouter.

25
00:01:52,407 --> 00:01:54,883
Your key stays on your device.

26
00:01:54,883 --> 00:01:58,257
Kofflard. Find the music you didn't know you were looking for.

